          "id": "http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416",
          "type": "Type",
          "_label": "Details (Official List Description)"
        }
      ],
      "content": "ALDBURY               STOCKS ROAD SP 9612                                        (West side) 12/15                                  Nos. 1, 3, 5, and 7                                        (Chantry Cottages) GV                                     II Block of 4 houses. C18, renovated c.1856 by Brownlow Estate extending S house (No. 1) as schoolmistress's house. Red brick and steep red tiled roofs, half-hipped at S. A block of 2-storeys and part attics houses set back from road facing E, with rear outshuts under catslide roofs. No. 1 has added rear parlour with small canted bay window on S with cast-iron lattice casements echoing that of S end of school.  2 large square internal chimneys serve the 4 houses. Each house has 2 1st floor windows and a larger ground floor window next the gabled open porch to the plank door. Yorkshire sliding casements with lattice leading, 2-light above, 3-light below. 2 small rear gabled dormers light attics. Interiors have chamfered tie-beams exposed and stud partitions infilled with brick. Included for group value. Listing NGR: SP9640312490"
    }
  ],
